Source: pve-triton-stack
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Nayef <nayef@local>
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)

Package: pve-triton-stack
Architecture: all
# pve-qemu-kvm carries the Triton quilt series since the 2026-10-08 pivot
# (pve-triton-qemu, the utmapp-fork coexistence package, is retired).
Depends: pve-triton-dxvk, pve-triton-virglrenderer, pve-qemu-kvm (>= 11.1.1-2+triton1), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Triton/Neptune D3D11 stack for Proxmox VE (meta package)
 Meta package tying together the Triton host stack: pve-triton-dxvk
 (host D3D11 renderer), pve-triton-virglrenderer (Neptune render server,
 system libvirglrenderer replacement) and pve-qemu-kvm carrying the
 Triton quilt series (Neptune-capable virtio-gpu). Ships only the
 /etc/pve-triton/env conffile documenting optional NPT_*_LIBRARY_PATH
 overrides; no wrapper is needed since the pivot (PVE launches
 /usr/bin/kvm directly and everything resolves system-wide).
